    {
      "bbox": [
        212,
        1508,
        1467,
        2094
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Proselyting of personnel by one City department or agency from the ranks of others, at the expense of others, has become a not uncommon practice. This practice puts one department in the position of bidding against another. This is a disruptive practice. The City government is unitary, and the departments and agencies are simply component parts of it. Except under special circumstances in which the qualifications of a particular individual are clearly more suited to an assignment in one department of agency than in another, the policy will be to disapprove such transfers.",
      "logprob_stats": {
